---
description: Build Curv OS screens with page shells from @curvgroup/design-system. Always on for UI work.
globs:
  - "**/*.tsx"
  - "**/*.jsx"
alwaysApply: true
---

This is a Curv OS app. UI comes from `@curvgroup/design-system`.

When the user asks for a screen, pick one shell (they will not name it):

- list / table / queue / catalog → `ListPage`
- one product / deal / customer / SKU → `DetailPage` (one record: verdict + max 4 vitals + tabs). Not a section home.
- overview / dashboard / home → `DashboardPage` (max 5 KPIs, max 2 charts)
- P&L / statement / landing-page performance → `ReportPage` (one chart + table, optional drawer)
- settings / form → `SettingsPage`

Tabs are not a default of three. One job that fits → no page tabs. Overflow or N named jobs → N tabs; each tab is still one shell. Copy `examples/dashboard-page.tsx` (one job) or `examples/dashboard-page-tabs.tsx` (two jobs). Chart + long table + row peek: `examples/report-page-performance.tsx`. Never invent Overview / Reporting / Marketing unless they named those jobs.

Copy `node_modules/@curvgroup/design-system/examples/<shell>.tsx`. Replace data. Do not add sections. Extra data goes in a tab, drawer, or hover — never a new card on the canvas. Showcase / `examples/` show the **full surface** of a component; drop unused slots rather than inventing a thinner private variant. Page titles are headline only (`title` + optional count/badge/actions — no eyebrow, no subtitle). Never hand-roll AppFrame, DataTable, or a page layout. Do not invent props. Sentence case; no CSS `uppercase`.
